  "limitations": [
    "API-07 is scoped to one local installation. Runtime authorization accepts authenticated human viewer, operator, approver, or admin roles, and the 43-instance status projection explicitly reports scope single-local-installation; this is not tenant isolation or a multi-installation authorization claim.",
    "API-07 is read-only. It exposes persisted cancellation metadata when present but does not implement POST /api/v1/runs/{run_id}/cancel, create a cancellation mutation seam, or claim worker cancellation behavior.",
    "DEL-04 owns Alembic migrations, bootstrap, upgrade, and historical backfill. API-07 adds feed_sequence and its counter to ORM metadata and proves metadata-created SQLite behavior; it does not claim migration or live PostgreSQL DDL/runtime parity, and the optional PostgreSQL driver test may skip when unavailable.",
    "DEL-05 owns default runnable composition. API-07 installs typed routes and fails closed when complete asynchronous resource executors are absent; tests inject real services or bounded fakes rather than claiming the default process constructs every repository, digest key, and catalog-backed service.",
    "Run detail reads bounded children in one unit of work, cross-validates their bindings, and rereads the parent Run to detect parent drift. API-07 does not claim that a default READ COMMITTED transaction gives a portable repeatable-read snapshot of every child row; deployment isolation and composition still require DEL-04 and DEL-05 verification.",
    "DEL-07 owns the committed OpenAPI snapshot, generated TypeScript client, and drift gate. API-07 verifies the live FastAPI document, stable operation IDs, typed schemas, and absence of a Run mutation, but does not claim generated client artifacts.",
    "API-09 still owns the process-wide application/problem+json vocabulary, shared correlation middleware, browser Origin, CSRF and Fetch-Metadata enforcement, trusted proxy policy, and global timeout and retry controls. API-07 supplies fixed route-local failures and private read-response headers but does not claim that larger boundary.",
    "API-07 conservatively re-redacts proposal payload fields, but the opaque destination summary and proposal values under neutral keys still rely on the producer's persisted redacted-projection contract. result_safe_metadata is omitted, not claimed safe; no privacy claim is made for arbitrary connector metadata.",
    "No live model provider, connector dispatch, repair, or retention-deletion job is exercised or claimed. Metadata expiry and unkeyed canonical fingerprints plus bounded sequence/coherence checks detect covered disagreement, but a trusted database administrator can rewrite rows and recompute those fingerprints. This evidence makes no tamper-proof persistence claim.",
    "The global feed integrity check is bounded to its authoritative counter/tail and the selected page. It detects a selected interior gap and exact-hydration tampering; historical filtered-out rows outside that bounded selection are not revalidated on each request."
  ]
